282-283-284-285-286	148,645,988,1748	282. Bulb, and, 283, leaf and flowers of Dicentra No. 1. 284. Flower, natural size. 285, 286. Same, taken to pieces.	A Dicentra plant: a finely cut leaf and a raceme of nodding flowers (283) on stalks rising from a small scaly bulb (282, lower right); a single two-spurred flower (284, lower left); above it the flower taken to pieces (285, 286): inner petals, stamens in two sets round the pistil, and the spurred outer petals.
287	1082,1420,1304,1750	287. Diagram of the flower of a Corydal.	A cross-section plan of a Corydal flower: two sepals outside, four petals in two pairs, the two sets of stamens either side of the central pistil.
288	1364,1411,1520,1748	283. One of the sets of stamens united.	One set of Fumitory-family stamens: three filaments joined into a single stalk below, each tipped with an anther, the middle one larger.
